TRIUMPH & TRAGEDY  (トラトラ)
→ 793.93  
→ Board Wargames

GMT Games, 2015  |  Design: Craig Besinque
Type: 3-player (also 2-player) geopolitical grand strategy
Period: 1936-1945 Europe  |  Play time: 4-6 hours
Map: area-movement Eurasia (Americas / Empire abstract)

FACTIONS (RIVALS)
AXIS     Fascist   Germany + Italy     starts armed, industry-strong
WEST     Capitalist Britain + France   (+USA later)  economy-strong, initially disarmed
USSR     Communist Soviet Union        population/resource deep, industry-limited

CORE VARIABLES
POP  Population  (cities / controlled minors)
RES  Resources   (oil, minerals, etc.)
IND  Industry    (factories; raised only by Investment cards)
PROD Production  = least of POP, RES, IND
     At Peace: ignore RES
     At War:   RES counts; can be Blockaded

Spend 1 PROD each on:
- unit steps / new cadres
- Action cards   (Diplomacy + Command)
- Investment cards (Tech + Factories)

DIPLOMACY ON MINORS
Influence markers:
1  Associate
2  Protectorate   (defensive pact)
3  Satellite      (full military ally; you use its POP/RES)

Attacking a Satellite = Declaration of War on its patron.
Peace Dividend chit each year you stay at Peace (secret 0-2).

YEAR STRUCTURE
New Year
  Victory check
  Production (build units / buy cards)
  Government (card play + diplomacy resolve)
Then 4 Seasons of movement / combat

VICTORY (any one)
Economic   25 VP at New Year check
           VP = current PROD + Peace Dividends + A-bomb levels
               +2 per enemy capital controlled  -1 per DoW issued
Military   Control two rival Main/Sub-Capitals at once
Atomic     Complete 4-stage A-bomb AND deliver it (air in range)
1945 end   Highest VP if nobody else has already won

SHORT / 1939 SCENARIO
Starts mid-setup after a special diplomacy placement round.
Used for faster teaching / lecture play.
Alliances, DoW timing, and whether the West opens a second
front become the decisive variables.
